  "general_formula": {
    "block_hilbert_series": "(1-t^q)*(1 - s*t^(s-1) + (s-1)*t^s)/(1-t)^4",
    "hypotheses": [
      "S = k[x0,x1,x2,x3].",
      "L_1,...,L_s are distinct linear forms.",
      "Every pair has rank 2.",
      "Every triple has rank at least 3; equivalently no three planes contain a line.",
      "No assumption is made that all fourfold intersections are empty; point concurrences of four or more planes are allowed.",
      "Q has degree q and is a non-zero-divisor on S/I_C."
    ],
    "line_skeleton_hilbert_series": "(1 - s*t^(s-1) + (s-1)*t^s)/(1-t)^4",
    "line_skeleton_resolution": "0 -> S(-s)^(s-1) -> S(-(s-1))^s -> I_C -> 0",
    "proof_route": [
      "Geramita-Harbourne-Migliore proper-meeting star-configuration results are used only as contextual literature and for the basic-double-link framework.",
      "The ideal identity I_C=(F/L_i)=intersection_{i<j}(L_i,L_j) is proved directly by induction using the basic-double-link exact sequence; the induction only needs that the new plane contains no existing line component, i.e. no three planes contain a line.",
      "The displayed Hilbert-Burch matrix verifies the codimension-two perfect resolution for the product-quotient generators."
    ],
